<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Ba Vi by Motorbike: Return-to-Hanoi Planning</h1>
<p>Every Ba Vi trip is two trips wearing one tank of fuel, and the second one, the long ride back east into the city, is the part riders plan least and remember longest. The return leg carries a tired rider, an afternoon sky, a machine that has already done a full day&rsquo;s work and a city that saves its heaviest traffic for exactly the hour a western rider arrives at its edge. This guide plans that leg properly, as its own trip with its own rules, rather than as the shapeless end of the mountain one.</p>
<p>The machine, the fuel for the ride home and the return-time conversation all start at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk answers the return questions this guide raises every day. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, read the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/hanoi-to-ba-vi-motorbike-route/">Ba Vi route guide</a>, see the fleet and the terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
